  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "26105568",
      "title": "Assigning Type Aliases",
      "lectureOrder": 756,
      "videoOrder": 696,
      "sourceHash": "20ac8dc45c83619a796f767570b044a1dddf8695c6a96b22b5615124c82954e9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.29,
          "en": "Instructor: Now, the more TypeScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.29,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "you're going to write, the higher the chances that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 10.17,
          "en": "at some point, you might be repeating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.17,
          "end": 11.7,
          "en": "some type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.7,
          "end": 15.06,
          "en": "And we're actually already doing this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.06,
          "end": 19.14,
          "en": "Here, for people, I'm saying that I want an array of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.14,
          "end": 22.95,
          "en": "this kind of object, so that I want an array full of objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.95,
          "end": 24.6,
          "en": "that have this structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.6,
          "end": 28.02,
          "en": "and that's the same object I have up here for person.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.02,
          "end": 32.52,
          "en": "The same type definition, just in the non-array form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.52,
          "end": 35.28,
          "en": "But the object type is the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.28,
          "end": 38.94,
          "en": "Now, you can, of course, duplicate the type definition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.94,
          "end": 40.8,
          "en": "but it's more realistic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.8,
          "end": 43.77,
          "en": "that you wanna avoid that duplication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.77,
          "end": 48.15,
          "en": "And for that, you can create a so-called type alias.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.15,
          "end": 51.51,
          "en": "You can define your own base type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.51,
          "end": 55.047,
          "en": "in which a more complex type definition is stored,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.047,
          "end": 59.43,
          "en": "and then use that type alias instead of repeating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.43,
          "end": 61.263,
          "en": "the entire type definitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.37,
          "end": 65.97,
          "en": "For that here, for example, before we use this object type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.97,
          "end": 70.2,
          "en": "for the first time here, we can define such a type alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.2,
          "end": 72.33,
          "en": "with the type keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 74.73,
          "en": "And that's a keyword which does not exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.73,
          "end": 77.7,
          "en": "in standard JavaScript, but which is added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.7,
          "end": 79.293,
          "en": "by TypeScript instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.49,
          "end": 84.06,
          "en": "Now, after this type keyword, you use any name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.06,
          "end": 88.71000000000001,
          "en": "of your choice, which will be your new type name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.71000000000001,
          "end": 91.023,
          "en": "For example, person, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.22,
          "end": 94.56,
          "en": "And then after the equal sign here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.56,
          "end": 96.45,
          "en": "you then have a type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.45,
          "end": 99.93,
          "en": "Because this is a pure TypeScript feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.93,
          "end": 103.25999999999999,
          "en": "this will basically be thrown out of the window",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.25999999999999,
          "end": 106.32,
          "en": "when the code is compiled to JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.32,
          "end": 108.45,
          "en": "So here, on the right side of the equal sign,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.45,
          "end": 113.13,
          "en": "it's not a JavaScript value, but instead, a type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.13,
          "end": 116.49000000000001,
          "en": "And that could be our object type definition here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 119.37,
          "en": "which I now store here in this person type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.37,
          "end": 123.6,
          "en": "And now in all those places where I used this object type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 126.6,
          "en": "I can use my alias instead now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.6,
          "end": 128.64,
          "en": "And it's therefore still the same type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.64,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "but I only define it once and then I can repeat it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 134.79,
          "en": "in all the places where I need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.79,
          "end": 137.97,
          "en": "And I can still also change it like I'm doing it down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.97,
          "end": 141.27,
          "en": "to use it just as person like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.27,
          "end": 144.48,
          "en": "or to use it as an array full of persons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 146.403,
          "en": "That also works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.66,
          "end": 151.38,
          "en": "And that's the very important feature of type aliases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.38,
          "end": 155.07,
          "en": "which can save you a lot of typing work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.07,
          "end": 158.55,
          "en": "and which can therefore make your code more concise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.55,
          "end": 160.44299999999998,
          "en": "and easier to maintain.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
